      <h1 id="editing-egress-firewall-ovn" class="group scroll-mt-20">Editing an egress firewall for a project<a href="#editing-egress-firewall-ovn" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">As a cluster administrator, you can modify network traffic rules for an existing egress firewall.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-egress-firewall-edit_editing-egress-firewall-ovn" class="group scroll-mt-20">Editing an EgressFirewall custom resource (CR)<a href="#nw-egress-firewall-edit_editing-egress-firewall-ovn" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">As a cluster administrator, you can update the egress firewall for a project.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>A cluster using the OVN-Kubernetes network plugin.</li>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You must log in to the cluster as a cluster administrator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Find the name of the <code>EgressFirewall</code> CR for the project. Replace <code>&lt;project&gt;</code> with the name of the project.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get -n <project> egressfirewall"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Optional: If you did not save a copy of the <code>EgressFirewall</code> object when you created the egress network firewall, enter the following command to create a copy.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get -n <project> egressfirewall <name> -o yaml > <filename>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Replace <code>&lt;project&gt;</code> with the name of the project. Replace <code>&lt;name&gt;</code> with the name of the object. Replace <code>&lt;filename&gt;</code> with the name of the file to save the YAML to.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      After making changes to the policy rules, enter the following command to replace the <code>EgressFirewall</code> CR. Replace <code>&lt;filename&gt;</code> with the name of the file containing the updated <code>EgressFirewall</code> CR.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc replace -f <filename>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
